{
 "_read_me": [
  "GATE Overflow tags every question with a subject and one or more topics.",
  "Those tags are far more reliable than guessing from keywords, so when a GO",
  "book is imported the tags are used first and content/topic_keywords.json is",
  "only a fallback.",
  "",
  "'topics' maps a GO tag straight to a subject/topic slug pair - best case.",
  "'subjects' maps a broader GO tag to just a subject, after which the keyword",
  "classifier picks the topic from within that subject only, which is much more",
  "accurate than searching all 101 topics.",
  "'ignore' lists tags that carry no syllabus meaning (difficulty labels, exam",
  "names, and so on).",
  "",
  "This mapping was written from GO's common tag vocabulary and is NOT complete.",
  "Run the importer with --audit-tags first: it reports every tag it saw that is",
  "not listed here, sorted by how often it appeared. Add the frequent ones and",
  "rerun. Fifteen minutes of this pays for itself."
 ],
